    "difficultyReason": "Calculate unequal colour probabilities and explain why three colours do not imply probability one third."
  },
  "content": {
    "id": "p12-q9-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "9",
    "prompt": {
      "format": "maths-editor-document-v1",
      "version": 1,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "id": "p12-q9-stem-1",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "fontSize": null,
          "align": "left",
          "spaceBefore": 0,
          "spaceAfter": 2,
          "lineHeight": 1.4,
          "indent": 0,
          "inlines": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "A bag of marbles contains 3 red marbles, 2 green marbles and 5 blue marbles.",
              "marks": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "p12-q9-stem-2",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "fontSize": null,
          "align": "left",
          "spaceBefore": 0,
          "spaceAfter": 2,
          "lineHeight": 1.4,
          "indent": 0,
          "inlines": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "A marble is chosen at random.",
              "marks": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p12-q9-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "What is the probability that a red marble is chosen?",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\frac{3}{10}$",
          "worked": "Total: $3+2+5=10$ marbles.\n$$P(\\mathrm{red})=\\frac{3}{10}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 12
      },
      {
        "id": "p12-q9-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": {
          "format": "maths-editor-document-v1",
          "version": 1,
          "blocks": [
            {
              "id": "p12-q9-b-prompt",
              "type": "paragraph",
              "fontSize": null,
              "align": "left",
              "spaceBefore": 0,
              "spaceAfter": 2,
              "lineHeight": 1.4,
              "indent": 0,
              "inlines": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "Explain why your answer to part ",
                  "marks": []
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "a",
                  "marks": [
                    "bold"
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": " is not ",
                  "marks": []
                },
                {
                  "type": "math",
                  "latex": "\\frac{1}{3}",
                  "display": false
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": ".",
                  "marks": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "The colours are not equally likely because there are different numbers of marbles of each colour.",
          "worked": "The individual marbles are equally likely to be selected, but the three colours are not. There are 3 red marbles out of 10, so $P(\\mathrm{red})=\\frac{3}{10}$, not $\\frac{1}{3}$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 14
      },
      {
        "id": "p12-q9-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "What is the probability that a blue marble is chosen? Answer as a percentage.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$50\\%$",
          "worked": "Total: $3+2+5=10$ marbles.\n$$\\begin{align*}P(\\mathrm{blue}) &= \\frac{5}{10}\\\\P(\\mathrm{blue}) &= \\frac{1}{2}\\\\P(\\mathrm{blue}) &= 0.5\\end{align*}$$\nPercentage: $(0.5\\times100)\\%=50\\%$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 14
      }
    ]
  },
